dcmon: agentless fleet monitor over SSH

> on startup, it loads all the hosts

host_type = [ "PROXMOX", "VM", "LXC", "NAS"]

[
    {
        "hostname": <string>,
        "type": <host_type>,
        "ip": <string>,
        "password": <string>,
        "flags": {
            "gpu": <bool>,
            "docker": <bool>
        }
    }
]

> on `status` command
    1. ssh concurrently on each machine
    2. read uptime
    3. read cpu %, temp
    4. read mem %
    5. read gpu %, temp (if flags.gpu == true)
    6. read docker stats (if flags.docker == true)
    7. display results

> on `status <hostname>`
    1. ssh into <host.ip>
    2. display `status` result for the given <hostname>

> on `watch`
    1. ssh concurrently on each machine
    2. display `status` result in a live preview

> on `watch <hostname>`
    1. ssh into <host.ip>
    2. display `status` result in a live preview
